# Server configuration. Copy to `.env` (install.sh does this for you).
# Everything is optional; the server runs with no integrations at all.
# Secrets belong in this file only — never commit it (it is gitignored).
#
# Paths are as the server sees them INSIDE the container: the host directory
# HUB_DATA_DIR is mounted at /data. Commented lines show the built-in default;
# uncomment a line to change it.

# ─── Docker and install.sh ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Host-side publish address. 127.0.0.1 = reachable from this machine only.
# Set 0.0.0.0 ONLY when a reverse proxy or VPN that authenticates sits in front.
HUB_BIND=127.0.0.1
# Host-side port. The container always listens on 8090 internally.
HUB_PORT=8090
# uid the container runs as. install.sh keeps it in step with the owner of
# HUB_DATA_DIR so the non-root container can write its database and keys.
HUB_UID=1000
# Host directory persisted into the container at /data (database, keys, uploads).
HUB_DATA_DIR=./data

# ─── Address ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The exact origin your browser or the app uses to reach this hub: scheme, host
# and port, e.g. https://hub.example.com. Passkeys are bound to the FIRST entry
# (comma list allowed), and the server refuses passkey setup while it is unset.
# The app needs https for anything but localhost — see docs/MESH.md.
HUB_ORIGIN=http://localhost:8090
# The server answers only to hostnames it knows (a DNS-rebinding defence): those
# in HUB_ORIGIN, plus localhost, 127.0.0.1 and ::1, plus this comma list. Add the
# hostname a mesh or proxy serves the hub on if it is not in HUB_ORIGIN, or a
# container name another service uses (e.g. hub-api). Ports are ignored.
HUB_ALLOWED_HOSTS=
# Hostname passkeys are scoped to. Blank = HUB_ORIGIN's hostname.
HUB_RP_ID=
# Base URL used in links the server sends out (the approvals notice).
HUB_PUBLIC_BASE=http://localhost:8090
# IANA timezone name (Europe/Berlin, America/Chicago). Not an abbreviation such
# as EDT: an unknown value logs a warning and falls back to UTC.
HUB_TZ=UTC

# ─── Passkey and device identity ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shown in the passkey prompt.
# HUB_RP_NAME=Hub
# HUB_USER_NAME=user
# HUB_USER_DISPLAY=the user
# HUB_USER_HANDLE=hub-user
# Where passkeys live. Device keys are stored beside it (devicekeys.json).
HUB_PASSKEYS=/data/hub/passkeys.json
# HUB_DEVICEKEYS=/data/hub/devicekeys.json
# Unix socket `./install.sh --pair` mints enrolment codes through.
# HUB_PAIR_SOCK=/data/hub/pair.sock
# Timings and limits for the Face ID gate and pairing.
# HUB_CHALLENGE_TTL_S=120
# HUB_TERM_SESSION_TTL_S=3600
# HUB_CHAT_SESSION_TTL_S=3600
# HUB_ENROLL_CODE_TTL_S=120
# HUB_ENROLL_CODE_MAX_ATTEMPTS=5
# HUB_ENROLL_CODE_ATTEMPT_WINDOW_S=30
# HUB_ENROLL_CODE_GLOBAL_MAX_ATTEMPTS=200

# ─── Assistant gateway (Hermes) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave blank to run without an assistant. For a gateway running on this machine
# (outside Docker) use http://host.docker.internal:8642 — docker-compose.yml maps
# that name to the host. Docker Desktop (macOS, Windows) forwards it to the host's
# loopback; on Linux it reaches the host's Docker bridge address, so the gateway
# must listen there (or on 0.0.0.0 behind a firewall), not only on 127.0.0.1.
HERMES_API_BASE=
HERMES_API_KEY=
# HERMES_AGENT_ID=hermes
# HERMES_AGENT_NAME=Xavier
# The gateway's run-file archive, relative to its data dir.
# HERMES_CRON_OUTPUT_DIR=cron/output
# The key this server and the gateway's Hub adapter share: the adapter presents it
# on /api/platform/hub/*, the server presents it on the gateway's events callback.
# install.sh creates it on first run (random, mode 600) at
# <HUB_DATA_DIR>/hub-platform/HUB_PLATFORM_KEY on the host, which is this path in
# the container. The server reads it from this file only. Give the Hermes
# hub-platform plugin the SAME key: the plugin reads HUB_PLATFORM_KEY_FILE, then
# HUB_PLATFORM_KEY, then $HERMES_HOME/hub-platform/HUB_PLATFORM_KEY.
# HUB_PLATFORM_KEY_FILE=/data/hub-platform/HUB_PLATFORM_KEY
# Optional hub-bridge sidecar for CLI-backed reads and writes. It is included in
# this repo (hub-bridge/) but OPT-IN: start it with `docker compose --profile
# bridge up -d`, then set the URL below. Blank = every bridge-backed panel is off.
# HUB_BRIDGE_URL=http://hub-bridge:8091
# HUB_BRIDGE_TIMEOUT_S=35
# The agent's container name, for the bridge's default (docker) exec mode.
# HERMES_CONTAINER=hermes
# The Hermes data dir (state.db, config.yaml, cron/) as the exec target sees it.
# HERMES_DATA_DIR=/opt/data
# Shared bearer key the hub sends to the bridge on every call. install.sh mints it
# at <HUB_DATA_DIR>/hub-bridge/HUB_BRIDGE_KEY (mode 600); the hub reads it from this
# file, never from an env var. Both the hub and the bridge read the SAME file.
# HUB_BRIDGE_KEY_FILE=/data/hub-bridge/HUB_BRIDGE_KEY

# ─── Chat ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HUB_CHAT_DB=/data/hub/chat/chat.db
# HUB_CHAT_MEDIA_DIR=/data/hub/chat/media
# HUB_CHAT_MEDIA_MAX_BYTES=2147483648
# HUB_CHAT_COMMAND_CATALOG=/data/hub/chat/commands-catalog.json
# HUB_CHAT_SESSIONS_FILE=/data/hub/chat/sessions.json
# HUB_CHAT_SEND_FORWARD_TIMEOUT_S=3
# HUB_CHAT_WS_POLL_INTERVAL_S=1.0
# HUB_CHAT_WS_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_S=15.0

# ─── Files the server reads ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Agents and scheduled jobs write these; a missing file is shown as "no data
# yet". Under Docker, point anything you wire up at a path below /data.
HUB_LOG_DIR=/data/hub/log
# How old a cached file may be before a read reports it stale (seconds).
# HUB_CACHE_MAX_AGE_S=900
# HUB_ACCESS_REPORT=~/.hub/access-report.json
# HUB_ROSTER=~/.hub/agents.json
# HUB_ACTIVITY=~/.hub/activity.json
# HUB_SCHEDULES=~/.hub/schedules.json
# HUB_SKILLS=~/.hub/skills.json
# MY_PAGES_ROOT=~/Sites/my-pages
# HUB_INBOX_DIR=/data/hub-inbox
# HUB_DECISIONS_DIR=/data/hub/decisions
# HUB_FINANCE_SNAPSHOT=/data/sites/finance/snapshot.json
# HUB_RECURRING_COSTS=/data/finance/recurring-costs.json
# HUB_MCP_WATCH_LOG=/data/hub/log/mcp-watch.jsonl
# HUB_CALENDAR=/data/hub/calendar.json
# HUB_CALENDAR_SYNC_REQUEST=/data/hub/calendar-sync.request
# HUB_TOPICS_CONFIG=/data/hub/config/telegram-topics.json
# HUB_TOPICS_LIVE=/data/hub/config/telegram-topics.live.json
# HUB_BRIEFING_DISMISSALS=/data/hub/data/briefing_dismissals.json
# HUB_BRIEFING_FEEDBACK=/data/hub/data/briefing_feedback.jsonl
# HUB_BRIEFING_RULES=/data/hub/data/briefing_rules.json
# HUB_BRIEF_DISMISS_KEY_FILE=/data/hub/data/brief_dismiss.key
# HUB_PUSH_TOKENS=/data/hub/data/push_tokens.json

# ─── File browser (/api/files) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Read-only roots, "id:label:/abs/path;id2:label2:/abs/path2". Credential-shaped
# names (.env, *.pem, *.key, *token*, *secret* …) are never served.
# HUB_FS_ROOTS=
# Without HUB_FS_ROOTS, each of these adds one root when set. None is served by
# default.
# HUB_FS_SITES=~/Sites
# HUB_FS_CODE=~/code
# HUB_FS_HUB_CONFIG=~/.hub
# HUB_FS_LAUNCH_AGENTS=~/Library/LaunchAgents

# ─── Terminal and Claude Code shells (opt-in: host/README.md) ─────────────────
# A real shell on this machine behind Face ID. Off until you run
# `sudo host/install.sh`; then uncomment these two (the gid is the one it
# printed) and run ./install.sh --restart. The override mounts /run/xavier
# read-only and sets HUB_TTYD_SOCK and HUB_TMUXD_SOCK for you.
# COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml:host/compose.host.yml
# XAVIER_HUB_GID=
# Only for a hub outside Docker: the sockets directly. Blank = off.
# HUB_TTYD_SOCK=
# HUB_TTYD_BASE=/terminal
# HUB_TMUXD_SOCK=

# ─── iMessage (an MCP server on your Mac) ─────────────────────────────────────
# IMESSAGE_MCP_URL=http://your-mac:8400/mcp
# The token, or a file holding it.
# IMESSAGE_MCP_TOKEN=
# IMESSAGE_TOKEN_FILE=/data/hub/secrets/imessage-token
# Drafts made while the Mac sleeps wait here.
# IMESSAGE_QUEUE_DIR=/data/hub/queue/imessage-drafts
# Per-install key for draft approval links (created on first use).
# COMPOSE_HMAC_FILE=/data/hub/secrets/compose-hmac
# HUB_IMESSAGE_ATTENTION_THREAD=home
# HUB_IMESSAGE_DRAFT_TTL_S=900

# ─── Discord approvals (Approve/Deny buttons for iMessage drafts) ─────────────
# Dormant until all three are set. The bot token lives in the file, not here.
# HUB_DISCORD_APPROVALS_TOKEN=/data/hub/secrets/discord-approvals-token
# HUB_APPROVALS_CHANNEL=
# HUB_APPROVER_DISCORD_ID=

# ─── Other integrations ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Home Assistant: leave false. True is reserved for a live-apply path that is
# not wired yet; the apply route refuses while it is set.
HA_LIVE_APPLY=false
# OpenRouter: the API key enables the credits card; the management key adds
# per-model activity.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_MGMT_KEY=
# OpenClaw CLI for the agents roster. Unset, it is never run.
# OPENCLAW_BIN=/opt/homebrew/bin/openclaw
